  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **rome wasn't built in a day** (1 review): Reviewer says this is really titled \"Orange\", originally by Furniture Huschle, and calls this version a strong rendition [4]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **talk some more about Jandek**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **learning the song**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **Alabama Nova**: back after 59 archived shows (3467 days); rare: 3 archived performances [6]\n- **introducing John Vanderslice**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **rome wasn't built in a day**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **I Miss the War**: mythic rare: 2 archived performances [6]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tmg2004-10-18** (recommended): source not stated; 21 songs; 78 min; rated 5/5 by 4 [1]. Said about its sound: Midway through the song the taper moved, and the recording got quieter for a while; otherwise fine [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: Jandek [1]\n- Peter Hughes played bass and sometimes sang backing vocals with the band [1]\n- John Vanderslice opened the night, and his full band joined the Mountain Goats onstage near the end [1]\n- Reviewer attended on their birthday, can be heard shouting on the recording, and drank with the singer for an hour afterward [3]\n- Reviewer says everyone in the room had a lot of energy [4]\n- Reviewer ranks this as their favorite Mountain Goats show ever and says it would win over newcomers [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **tmg2004-10-18**: taped by Brandon; transferred by Brandon; source: Sony MZ-NH900 portable minidisc recorder (in PCM mode) with binaural cardoid microphones [1]",
